/-!
# Persistence of nondegenerate critical points on a manifold

A nondegenerate critical point `x` of a real function `f` on a boundaryless finite-dimensional
manifold survives every sufficiently small `C²` perturbation, together with its Morse index.

The perturbation is measured on a fixed compact coordinate set. Fix a chart `e` of the `C²`
maximal atlas around `x`. For every sufficiently small radius `r` there is `δ > 0` such that each
function `g`, `C²` on the inverse image `K` of the closed coordinate ball of radius `r` around the
chart image of `x`, whose coordinate differential at that point has norm at most `δ` and whose
coordinate second derivative is within `δ` of that of `f` on the ball, has exactly one critical
point in `K`. That critical point is nondegenerate, has the Morse index of `x`, and its position
and critical value are controlled by the coordinate differential of `g` at the chart image of `x`
(`IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint.exists_criticalPoint_perturbation_manifoldMorseIndex_eq`).

For `C^n` maps with `n ≥ 2` and the weak Whitney topology, generated by compact chart derivative
tests, this says that `x` has arbitrarily small compact neighbourhoods `K` such that every map `g`
near `f` has exactly one critical point in `K`; it is nondegenerate with the Morse index of `x`,
and it tends to `x`, with critical value tending to `f x`, as `g` tends to `f`
(`TauCeti.IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint.exists_mem_nhds_eventually_criticalPoint`).

Both statements are read off from the vector-space theorem
`TauCeti.IsNondegenerateCriticalPoint.exists_criticalPoint_perturbation_morseIndex_eq` in one
chart, using that nondegeneracy, criticality and the Morse index may be computed in any chart of
the maximal atlas.

## References

* M. Audin and M. Damian, *Morse Theory and Floer Homology*, Springer Universitext, 2014,
  Chapter 1.
* J. Milnor, *Lectures on the h-cobordism theorem*, Princeton University Press, 1965, §2.
-/

public section

open Filter Metric Set
open scoped Manifold Topology ContDiff

namespace TauCeti

variable {E H M : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
  [TopologicalSpace H] {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} [I.Boundaryless]
  [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M] {x : M}

/-- **Persistence of a nondegenerate critical point on a manifold, in a chart.**

Let `x` be a nondegenerate critical point of `f` on a boundaryless finite-dimensional manifold and
`e` a chart of the `C²` maximal atlas at `x`. For every sufficiently small `r`, the closed ball of
radius `r` around `e.extend I x` lies in the chart target, and there is `δ > 0` with the following
property. Let `g` be `C²` on the inverse image of that ball, with coordinate differential of norm
at most `δ` at `e.extend I x`, and with coordinate second derivative within `δ` of that of `f` on
the ball. Then `g` has exactly one critical point `y` in the inverse image of the ball. It is
nondegenerate with the Morse index of `x`, its chart image lies within `K * ‖dg‖` of that of `x`,
and `|g y - g x| ≤ K * ‖dg‖ ^ 2`, where `dg` is the coordinate differential of `g` at
`e.extend I x` and `K` depends only on `f`, `x` and `e`. -/
theorem IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint.exists_criticalPoint_perturbation_manifoldMorseIndex_eq
    {f : M → ℝ} {e : OpenPartialHomeomorph M H} (he : e ∈ IsManifold.maximalAtlas I 2 M)
    (hx : x ∈ e.source) (h : IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint I f x) :
    ∃ K : ℝ, ∀ᶠ r in 𝓝[>] 0, closedBall (e.extend I x) r ⊆ (e.extend I).target ∧
      ∃ δ > 0, ∀ g : M → ℝ,
        (∀ y ∈ (e.extend I).symm '' closedBall (e.extend I x) r, ContMDiffAt I 𝓘(ℝ) 2 g y) →
        ‖fderiv ℝ (g ∘ (e.extend I).symm) (e.extend I x)‖ ≤ δ →
        (∀ z ∈ closedBall (e.extend I x) r,
          ‖fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (g ∘ (e.extend I).symm)) z -
            fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (f ∘ (e.extend I).symm)) z‖ ≤ δ) →
        ∃ y ∈ (e.extend I).symm '' closedBall (e.extend I x) r,
          IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint I g y ∧
          manifoldMorseIndex I g y = manifoldMorseIndex I f x ∧
          dist (e.extend I y) (e.extend I x) ≤
            K * ‖fderiv ℝ (g ∘ (e.extend I).symm) (e.extend I x)‖ ∧
          |g y - g x| ≤ K * ‖fderiv ℝ (g ∘ (e.extend I).symm) (e.extend I x)‖ ^ 2 ∧
          ∀ z ∈ (e.extend I).symm '' closedBall (e.extend I x) r,
            z ∈ criticalPoints I g → z = y := by
  have hxs : x ∈ (e.extend I).source := by rwa [e.extend_source]
  obtain ⟨K, hK⟩ := ((isManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint_iff_of_mem_maximalAtlas he hx).1
    h).exists_criticalPoint_perturbation_morseIndex_eq
  refine ⟨K, ?_⟩
  have htarget : (e.extend I).target ∈ 𝓝 (e.extend I x) :=
    e.isOpen_extend_target.mem_nhds ((e.extend I).map_source hxs)
  filter_upwards [hK, nhdsWithin_le_nhds (eventually_closedBall_subset htarget)]
    with r ⟨δ, hδ, hr⟩ hsub
  refine ⟨hsub, δ, hδ, fun g hg hgx hgf ↦ ?_⟩
  -- Points of the ball come from the chart source, and the chart undoes its inverse there.
  have hsource {z : E} (hz : z ∈ closedBall (e.extend I x) r) :
      (e.extend I).symm z ∈ e.source := by
    rw [← e.extend_source (I := I)]
    exact (e.extend I).map_target (hsub hz)
  have hright {z : E} (hz : z ∈ closedBall (e.extend I x) r) :
      e.extend I ((e.extend I).symm z) = z :=
    (e.extend I).right_inv (hsub hz)
  have hg' : ∀ z ∈ closedBall (e.extend I x) r, ContDiffAt ℝ 2 (g ∘ (e.extend I).symm) z :=
    fun z hz ↦ by
      simpa only [hright hz] using (contMDiffAt_iff_contDiffAt_comp_extend_symm he
        (hsource hz)).1 (hg _ (mem_image_of_mem _ hz))
  obtain ⟨y, hy, hynd, hyind, hdist, hval, huniq⟩ := hr (g ∘ (e.extend I).symm) hg' hgx hgf
  have hgy : IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint I g ((e.extend I).symm y) :=
    (isManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint_iff_of_mem_maximalAtlas he (hsource hy)).2
      (by rwa [hright hy])
  refine ⟨(e.extend I).symm y, mem_image_of_mem _ hy, hgy, ?_, by rwa [hright hy], ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [manifoldMorseIndex_eq_morseIndex_of_mem_maximalAtlas he (hsource hy) hgy.contMDiffAt
      hgy.mvfderiv_eq_zero, manifoldMorseIndex_eq_morseIndex_of_mem_maximalAtlas he hx
      h.contMDiffAt h.mvfderiv_eq_zero, hright hy]
    exact hyind
  · simpa only [Function.comp_apply, e.extend_left_inv hx] using hval
  · rintro _ ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩ hcrit
    have hzero := (mvfderiv_eq_zero_iff_fderiv_comp_extend_symm_eq_zero
      (IsManifold.maximalAtlas_subset_of_le (by norm_num) he) (hsource hz)
      ((hg _ (mem_image_of_mem _ hz)).mdifferentiableAt two_ne_zero)).1
        (TauCeti.mem_criticalPoints.1 hcrit)
    rw [hright hz] at hzero
    rw [huniq z hz hzero]

section WeakWhitney

open scoped TauCeti.ManifoldWeakWhitney

variable {n : ℕ∞ω} [IsManifold I n M]

/-- For a `C^n` function `f` with `n ≥ 2` whose coordinate differential vanishes at the chart
image of `x` in the preferred chart, every map near `f` in the weak Whitney topology satisfies the
`δ`-hypotheses of the chart persistence theorem on a closed coordinate ball in the chart target. -/
private theorem eventually_perturbation_hypotheses {f : C^n⟮I, M; 𝓘(ℝ), ℝ⟯} (hn : 2 ≤ n)
    (hf : fderiv ℝ (f ∘ (extChartAt I x).symm) (extChartAt I x x) = 0) {r : ℝ}
    (hr : closedBall (extChartAt I x x) r ⊆ (extChartAt I x).target) {δ : ℝ} (hδ : 0 < δ) :
    ∀ᶠ g : C^n⟮I, M; 𝓘(ℝ), ℝ⟯ in 𝓝 f,
      ‖fderiv ℝ (g ∘ (extChartAt I x).symm) (extChartAt I x x)‖ ≤ δ ∧
      ∀ z ∈ closedBall (extChartAt I x x) r,
        ‖fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (g ∘ (extChartAt I x).symm)) z -
          fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (f ∘ (extChartAt I x).symm)) z‖ ≤ δ := by
  have hT : IsOpen (extChartAt I x).target := isOpen_extChartAt_target x
  -- The differential at the chart image of `x` tends to that of `f`, which vanishes.
  have h1 : Tendsto (fun g : C^n⟮I, M; 𝓘(ℝ), ℝ⟯ ↦
      fderiv ℝ (g ∘ (extChartAt I x).symm) (extChartAt I x x)) (𝓝 f) (𝓝 0) := by
    have h := (tendsto_fderivWithin_extChartAt (f₀ := f) (y := (0 : ℝ)) (one_le_two.trans hn)
      (mem_extChartAt_target x) (by simp)).comp
        (tendsto_id.prodMk (tendsto_const_nhdsWithin (mem_extChartAt_target x)))
    have hL : fderivWithin ℝ (extChartAt 𝓘(ℝ) (0 : ℝ) ∘ f ∘ (extChartAt I x).symm)
        (extChartAt I x).target (extChartAt I x x) = 0 := by
      rw [extChartAt_model_space_eq_id, PartialEquiv.refl_coe, Function.id_comp,
        fderivWithin_of_isOpen hT (mem_extChartAt_target x), hf]
    rw [hL] at h
    refine h.congr fun g ↦ ?_
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, id_eq, extChartAt_model_space_eq_id, PartialEquiv.refl_coe,
      Function.id_comp]
    exact fderivWithin_of_isOpen hT (mem_extChartAt_target x)
  -- On the compact ball, second coordinate derivatives of nearby maps converge uniformly.
  have h2 : TendstoUniformlyOn (fun (g : C^n⟮I, M; 𝓘(ℝ), ℝ⟯) w ↦
      fderivWithin ℝ (fderivWithin ℝ (g ∘ (extChartAt I x).symm) (extChartAt I x).target)
        (extChartAt I x).target w)
      (fun w ↦ fderivWithin ℝ (fderivWithin ℝ (f ∘ (extChartAt I x).symm) (extChartAt I x).target)
        (extChartAt I x).target w) (𝓝 f) (closedBall (extChartAt I x x) r) := by
    simpa only [extChartAt_model_space_eq_id, PartialEquiv.refl_coe, Function.id_comp] using
      tendstoUniformlyOn_fderivWithin_fderivWithin_extChartAt (f₀ := f) (y := (0 : ℝ)) hn
        (isCompact_closedBall _ r) hr (by simp)
  filter_upwards [h1.eventually (closedBall_mem_nhds 0 hδ),
    (Metric.tendstoUniformlyOn_iff (α := E →L[ℝ] E →L[ℝ] ℝ)).1 h2 δ hδ] with g hg1 hg2
  refine ⟨by simpa using hg1, fun z hz ↦ ?_⟩
  have := hg2 z hz
  -- On the open chart target, derivatives within the target are ordinary derivatives.
  rw [fderivWithin_fderivWithin_eq_of_mem_nhds (hT.mem_nhds (hr hz)),
    fderivWithin_fderivWithin_eq_of_mem_nhds (hT.mem_nhds (hr hz)), dist_comm] at this
  exact ((dist_eq_norm (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (g ∘ (extChartAt I x).symm)) z)
    (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (f ∘ (extChartAt I x).symm)) z)).symm.trans_lt this).le

/-- **Persistence of a nondegenerate critical point in the weak Whitney topology.**

Let `x` be a nondegenerate critical point of a `C^n` function `f`, `n ≥ 2`, on a boundaryless
finite-dimensional manifold. Inside every neighbourhood `V` of `x` there is a compact
neighbourhood `K` of `x` such that every map `g` near `f` in the weak Whitney topology has exactly
one critical point `y` in `K`; it is nondegenerate, has the Morse index of `x`, and it lies in any
prescribed neighbourhood `U` of `x`, with `g y` in any prescribed neighbourhood `W` of `f x`, once
`g` is close enough to `f`. -/
theorem IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint.exists_mem_nhds_eventually_criticalPoint
    {f : C^n⟮I, M; 𝓘(ℝ), ℝ⟯} (hn : 2 ≤ n) (h : IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint I f x)
    {V : Set M} (hV : V ∈ 𝓝 x) :
    ∃ K ∈ 𝓝 x, K ⊆ V ∧ IsCompact K ∧ ∀ U ∈ 𝓝 x, ∀ W ∈ 𝓝 (f x),
      ∀ᶠ g : C^n⟮I, M; 𝓘(ℝ), ℝ⟯ in 𝓝 f, ∃ y ∈ K ∩ U, g y ∈ W ∧
        IsManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint I g y ∧
        manifoldMorseIndex I g y = manifoldMorseIndex I f x ∧
        ∀ z ∈ K, z ∈ criticalPoints I g → z = y := by
  have : IsManifold I 2 M := IsManifold.of_le hn
  obtain ⟨_, hK⟩ := h.exists_criticalPoint_perturbation_manifoldMorseIndex_eq
    (e := chartAt H x) (IsManifold.chart_mem_maximalAtlas x) (mem_chart_source H x)
  have hf := ((isManifoldNondegenerateCriticalPoint_iff I).1 h).fderiv_eq_zero
  have hsymm {s : Set M} (hs : s ∈ 𝓝 x) : (extChartAt I x).symm ⁻¹' s ∈ 𝓝 (extChartAt I x x) :=
    (continuousAt_extChartAt_symm x).preimage_mem_nhds (by rwa [extChartAt_to_inv])
  have hpos : ∀ᶠ r in 𝓝[>] (0 : ℝ), 0 < r := eventually_mem_nhdsWithin
  have hsmall {s : Set E} (hs : s ∈ 𝓝 (extChartAt I x x)) :
      ∀ᶠ r in 𝓝[>] (0 : ℝ), closedBall (extChartAt I x x) r ⊆ s :=
    eventually_nhdsWithin_of_eventually_nhds (eventually_closedBall_subset hs)
  obtain ⟨r, hr0, hrV, hrT, δ, hδ, hr⟩ := (hpos.and ((hsmall (hsymm hV)).and hK)).exists
  refine ⟨(extChartAt I x).symm '' closedBall (extChartAt I x x) r, ?_, image_subset_iff.2 hrV,
    (isCompact_closedBall _ r).image_of_continuousOn ((continuousOn_extChartAt_symm x).mono hrT),
    fun U hU W hW ↦ ?_⟩
  · filter_upwards [extChartAt_source_mem_nhds (I := I) x,
      (continuousAt_extChartAt (I := I) x).preimage_mem_nhds (closedBall_mem_nhds _ hr0)]
      with y hys hy
    exact ⟨extChartAt I x y, hy, (extChartAt I x).left_inv hys⟩
  -- Nearby maps take values in `W` at the points near `x` in some neighbourhood `U'`.
  obtain ⟨pa, hpa, pb, hpb, hpab⟩ := eventually_prod_iff.1 <| show
      ∀ᶠ p : C^n⟮I, M; 𝓘(ℝ), ℝ⟯ × M in 𝓝 f ×ˢ 𝓝 x, p.1 p.2 ∈ W by
    rw [← nhds_prod_eq]
    exact ContMDiffMap.continuous_eval_manifoldWeakWhitney.continuousAt.preimage_mem_nhds hW
  -- A smaller admissible radius whose ball lies in `U ∩ U'`.
  obtain ⟨r', hr'U, hr'r, -, δ', hδ', hr'⟩ := ((hsmall (hsymm (inter_mem hU hpb))).and
    ((hsmall (closedBall_mem_nhds _ hr0)).and hK)).exists
  have hC2 (g : C^n⟮I, M; 𝓘(ℝ), ℝ⟯) (y : M) : ContMDiffAt I 𝓘(ℝ) 2 g y :=
    (g.contMDiff.of_le hn).contMDiffAt
  filter_upwards [hpa, eventually_perturbation_hypotheses hn hf hrT hδ,
    eventually_perturbation_hypotheses hn hf (hr'r.trans hrT) hδ'] with g hga hg hg'
  obtain ⟨y, hyK, hy, hyind, -, -, huniq⟩ := hr g (fun y _ ↦ hC2 g y) hg.1 hg.2
  obtain ⟨y', hy'K, hy', -, -, -, -⟩ := hr' g (fun y _ ↦ hC2 g y) hg'.1 hg'.2
  -- By uniqueness in the larger ball, the critical point found in the smaller ball is `y`.
  obtain rfl := huniq y' (image_mono hr'r hy'K) hy'.mem_criticalPoints
  obtain ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩ := hy'K
  exact ⟨_, ⟨hyK, (hr'U hz).1⟩, hpab hga (hr'U hz).2, hy, hyind, huniq⟩

end WeakWhitney

end TauCeti
